            <ArticleTitle>A case of DIPNECH presenting as usual interstitial pneumonia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>174-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5603/PiAP.2016.0020</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Diffuse idiopathic pulmonary neuroendocrine cell hyperplasia (DIPNECH) is a rare disease that is classically described as presenting with cough, dyspnea, and wheezing in non-smoker middle aged females. Pulmonary function tests commonly demonstrate an obstructive pattern and CT of chest usually reveals diffuse air trapping with mosaic pattern. We present a case of patient with DIPNECH manifesting with restrictive pattern and as usual interstitial pneumonia on imaging.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
